ant","dish/campisi-s-egyptian-restaurant"],["Cannelloni","dish/cannelloni"],["Capellini","dish/capellini"]]}]},"dish/garbure":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/garbure","n":"Garbure","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Garbure is a savoury French dish, described either as a soup or a stew.  It is a one-pot dish of vegetables – mainly root vegetables – with one or more of several meats, slowly cooked in an earthenware dish in an oven. The cooking liquid is sometimes served as soup before the meat and vegetables are served as a main course. The food writer Curnonsky named garbure as one of the four great regional dishes of France."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-garbure"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garbure"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Ham","ingredient/ham"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","ref":"site/pardonyourfrench-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","ref":"site/lacuisinedegeraldine-fr","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true},{"name":"New Caledonia Tourism: Kanak cooking","ref":"site/newcaledonia-travel","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newcaledonia.travel","note":"Official tourism board overview of Kanak food, including bougna cooked in an earth oven.","url":"https://www.newcaledonia.travel/nz/gastronomy-wine/gastronomy/kanak-cooking","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from French 